## 4.2 Note 1c Asymmetric Logic Concern

**Severity:** ⚠️ **MEDIUM** - Logic is correct but potentially confusing

**Issue:** Note 1c has asymmetric behavior where meeting criteria in some firecells doesn't grant exemption if ANY firecell fails.

**Regulatory Text (CAS2 Page 35, Note 1c):**
> "This system is not required where the building is single level and all areas of Occupancy WB have storage with a height not greater than 3 m and have an occupant load not exceeding 50"

**Current Implementation Logic:**

```javascript
// Note 1c: ALL WB firecells must meet BOTH criteria
const allWBOnSameFloor = wbFirecells.every(fc => fc.floor === floor);
const allMeetCriteria = wbFirecells.every(
  fc => (fc.maxStorageHeight || 0) < 3 && (fc.maxEscapeRouteOccupants || 0) <= 50
);

const exempt = allWBOnSameFloor && allMeetCriteria;
