## 5.6 Architectural Questions Requiring Decisions

### 5.6.1 Harmonization Order of Operations

**Question:** Should harmonization happen BEFORE or AFTER note evaluations?

**Option A: Harmonize BEFORE notes**
- Pro: Notes evaluate on final, harmonized systems
- Pro: More stringent systems get note benefits (e.g., FENZ exemption)
- Con: Notes may remove systems that were harmonized (counterintuitive)

**Option B: Harmonize AFTER notes**
- Pro: Notes evaluate on base systems only (simpler logic)
- Pro: Harmonization applies to already-modified systems
- Con: Harmonized systems miss note evaluations

**Recommendation:** Investigate current implementation, document decision, add tests validating chosen approach.

**Priority:** MEDIUM (needed before harmonization tests)

### 5.6.2 Note 1c Building-Wide vs Per-Firecell Interpretation

**Question:** Should Note 1c exemption be building-wide or per-firecell?

**Current Implementation:** Building-wide (if ANY WB firecell exceeds limits, NO WB firecells get exemption)

**Alternative:** Per-firecell (each WB firecell evaluated independently)

**Regulatory Text:** "...all areas of Occupancy WB..." suggests building-wide

**Recommendation:** Document current interpretation with rationale, consider regulatory clarification request

**Priority:** MEDIUM (correct but should be documented)

### 5.6.3 Addition Notes Evaluation Timing

**Question:** Should addition notes (7, 10) ALWAYS evaluate, or only when base systems reference the note?

**Current Implementation:** Addition notes appear to always evaluate (need confirmation)

**Regulatory Intent:** Notes 7 and 10 ADD systems that may not be in base lookup tables

**Recommendation:** Document that addition notes are special case, always evaluate regardless of base system codes

**Priority:** LOW (implementation appears correct, just needs documentation)

